1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,000
People's goals and barriers change week to week.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
Generic reminders don't show what they know about you, or why they suggest something.

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:16,600
A synthetic check-in starts as one plain sentence.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,600
It proposes 3 values, each with the words it came from. Mood gave none.

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,600
Sleep is corrected to 6.5 hours; the other two are confirmed.

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,400
Nothing is saved until the review is submitted.

7
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:33,180
Saved values update the Health Clone Passport.

8
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:38,180
The evidence thread traces one value from the check-in to the card.

9
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:42,380
A card with no value in 14 days is withheld, not guessed.

10
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:48,250
Inclinations: what weighs most for this member, from 7 short questions (simulated answers).

11
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:54,650
Each next step is linked to one of them, with its reason. A prompt for the care team, not a care plan.

12
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:58,490
After a pain report, the next step routes to a person.

13
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:01,890
The person can choose, defer or ask a professional.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,200
Crisis language is not processed.

15
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:10,500
A fixed hand-off points to a person. Nothing is saved.

16
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:16,480
The timeline shows what each saved check-in changed.

17
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:21,760
The research console leads with its results, in plain language.

18
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:26,660
Training runs offline. No AI model is used in the check-in loop.

19
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:31,990
Each training step was tested on the same 141 held-out practice prompts.

20
00:01:31,990 --> 00:01:38,390
With simulated members, the learned approach logged 84.0% of days, against 83.3% for the best fixed one.

21
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:44,230
On 141 held-out synthetic prompts, the base model passed 45.

22
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:49,230
Both fine-tuned stages passed all 141. 90 base replies were empty.

23
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:54,030
These are simulated results, not patient outcomes.

24
00:01:54,130 --> 00:01:59,830
7 questions recover simulated members' hidden traits 76–91% of the time.

25
00:01:59,830 --> 00:02:05,330
The reward model reads term by term. Its top message type matches the simulator's for 83%.

26
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:10,630
The learned policy gains a little: 0.840 against 0.833. Synthetic only, no new spend.

27
00:02:10,730 --> 00:02:16,930
Live: check-in, safety checks, proposals, review, memory, passport.

28
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:23,230
Offline: synthetic members, evaluation, training, frozen comparison.

29
00:02:23,330 --> 00:02:30,030
Synthetic data only. No diagnosis, treatment or dosing. No clinical review.

30
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:36,830
The rules caught 74 of 74 test violations: a measurement, not a proof.

31
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:42,630
It runs today as a hosted prototype.

32
00:02:42,630 --> 00:02:48,430
Reaching people needs consent, privacy, clinical oversight and a study first.

33
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:54,230
Next: a clinical reviewer, a consented pilot and a pre-registered measure.

34
00:02:54,230 --> 00:03:00,230
The prototype link is in the submission.
